id: pm-v53h9j
title: "GH-1264: enforce next ready-queue token budgets and disclose omitted recommendations"
description: "The SDK computes context packing but returns the complete ranking instead of the packed rows. Explicit token budgets therefore do not bound ready output, and the normal receipt hides the discarded packing decision. Restore binding rendered ready-queue accounting, truthful budget receipts, and SDK/CLI/MCP acceptance."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:cli","area:sdk",context-management,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-09-17T19:26:35.525Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-17T21:28:38.889Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-17T21:28:38.255Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-17T21:28:38.255Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Explicit budgets bound the documented ready-selection scope; omitted recommendation and rows are disclosed; selection and usage feedback agree with delivered rows; SDK, CLI and MCP preserve the contract; regressions fail before implementation and pass afterward."
parent: pm-5t33or
resolution: "Enforce ordered rendered ready-selection budgets, expose independent row-cap and token omissions, preserve emitted-row attribution, and document recovery."
expected_result: Bounded SDK/CLI/MCP selections disclose all omissions and remain efficient under strict gates.
actual_result: 8974 tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; static/type/token gates and fresh npm/Bun/npx/bunx/SDK/MCP acceptance pass; both review regressions pass.
