comments[16]:
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T19:26:35.525Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Duplicate check: live all-status searches for 1264, token budget, and next budget; read pm-55ra, pm-5t33or, pm-lixy, pm-atfm, and pm-1wujzi. No existing issue owns GH-1264. Existing packer history is retained as completed lineage; the new regression belongs under the binding-output contract."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T19:31:06.054Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "TDD evidence: added an isolated SDK regression with three real items. Before implementation the 10-token request still returned a recommendation; 21 existing tests passed and the new test failed. The fix explicitly distinguishes ready-selection budgets from whole-response budgets and discloses when even the empty structured selection exceeds a tiny budget."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T19:41:42.055Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Repository health snapshot: no open PRs; GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning open-alert inventories are empty; pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities and tracked-file credential scan passes. GH-1264 is linked here; GH-1246 already has its own canonical PM link in its GitHub comment. Scheduled Auto Release run 35197095403 succeeded for v2026.9.17; npm and GitHub agree. Latest pm-changelog is 2026.9.16. Sentry 14-day gate passed with critical=0, high=0; this is separate from final physical telemetry queue drain proof."
    edited_at: "2026-09-17T20:12:03.654Z"
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T19:51:19.212Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Installed-artifact acceptance passed in unrelated temporary projects: npm and Bun installs, SDK next, CLI next, npx and bunx all enforce a 32-token selection ceiling while preserving total ready counts; roomy and execute-intent reads retain the highest-ranked claimed task. Both installed MCP servers disclose omitted recommendations. Create/claim/update/comment/close/release/validate lifecycle, README cold start, Git merge reconciliation with strict history verification, and detached telemetry collector plus zero physical queue all passed. Temporary roots were removed."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T19:58:52.800Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full verification: all 704 test files and 8974 tests passed. Exact coverage gate reports statements 64762/64762, branches 49402/49402, functions 13443/13443, lines 61992/61992 (100/100/100/100; zero uncovered counts). Existing token-budget gate passed 32 surfaces and infeasible-intent negative control; existing intent calibration passed at 2 and 2243 items without baseline relaxation. A linked focused run queued behind the full-suite lease and timed out; its serialized rerun is the authoritative linked-test result."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:12:04.275Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Graph evidence: the implementation contributes to the context-quality feature; the read-only health verification reconfirms the completed historical evidence-recovery result; bulk occupancy remains an adjacent unclaimed context-read problem with different prerequisites. The unrelated onboarding GitHub report keeps its canonical owner in its own issue comment. No ordering dependency or depth-only edge was invented."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:12:39.237Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Repository static verification passed ESLint after flattening the budget-search control flow, all three clone checks, repository static/docstring assertions, token and intent budgets, documentation, package boundaries, SDK parity, grammar/flags/recovery, agent token surfaces, MCP deprecation inventory, tracker measurements, gate registry and SDK transport/entrypoint costs. The final graph stage initially identified four new prose references; their semantic ownership was corrected through PM, then graph-composition and record-integrity both passed without changing any bound."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:13:06.363Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh operations verification: required-mode Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero critical/high issues, telemetry finish-error rate 1.47 percent below the existing 6 percent ceiling, and zero missing error-code rows. Live Sentry logs returned timestamps and trace identifiers from this session. GitHub alert APIs and pnpm audit remain empty. Scheduled release run 35197095403 actually published 2026.9.17 and verified npm/npx/bunx; no second automatic release is initiated by this delivery."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:25:36.077Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final packed rerun passed against the simplified build for npm/Bun SDK and CLI, npx/bunx executors, MCP, lifecycle/history, README cold start and detached telemetry. An additional unrelated strict TypeScript consumer compiled the installed public NextResult ready-budget receipt using the SDK whole-output omission union correctly; the guide now demonstrates that narrowing. This preserves honest refusal handling for package authors rather than asserting every budgeted read returns a normal result."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:28:56.799Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final source proof after control-flow simplification: 704 files and 8974 tests passed in 631 seconds. Exact counters: statements 64762/64762, branches 49404/49404, functions 13443/13443, lines 61992/61992; zero uncovered counts. Final packed runtime and strict TypeScript consumers passed. All local static stages and unchanged graph/record assertions passed. Hosted exact-head checks and review follow in the delivery PR."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:33:23.330Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1265 carries the implementation, SDK surface receipt, full validation evidence, structured closure and package-generated changelog. Implementation commit: 6a5e6826a. Exact-head hosted checks and bot feedback are retained on that PR; merge remains conditional on required checks and resolution of actionable findings."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:53:59.772Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "PR 1265 review TDD: two new row-limit assertions failed before the correction (ready_total was absent for roomy explicit budgets and advisory packing). The SDK now discloses the full ready population independently of selection-budget omissions."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T20:59:22.916Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The row-limit receipt added 18 bytes to the 2,243-item orientation session and correctly failed its no-growth ratchet. Shortened redundant recommendation wording while retaining readiness, priority and highest-priority meaning; the calibration baseline and limits remain unchanged. Complexity remains under the existing limit by handling the count in the established truncation builder."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T21:06:08.760Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "The later composed agent-task token gate also caught four extra tokens in orientation-contracts-next. The final wording uses ready / resume work and concise pN priority labels; the item status already carries open versus in-progress. No token baselines, suppression files, or limits were changed. Earlier static stages passed; the failing composed gate and remaining stages are being rerun before closeout."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T21:08:07.281Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Measured baseline review: the compact next projection omits prose reasons, so its necessary ready_total field costs 722 versus 718 tokens. Adopted the exact generated task baseline: contracts 4111 to 4108, orientation task 4829 to 4830, refusal 440 to 433, composite 12667 to 12661. Canonical orientation winner remains 1102. This corrects the preceding expectation that wording alone could offset the compact projection; no predicate, absolute budget, transcript, or negative control was relaxed."
  - created_at: "2026-09-17T21:28:37.000Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final pre-merge review verification: 8974 tests across 704 files pass; exact coverage 64764/64764 statements, 49406/49406 branches, 13443/13443 functions, 61994/61994 lines. Both CodeRabbit findings have failing-before/passing-after regression evidence. All static stages, typechecks, unchanged orientation calibration, refreshed composed-task ratchet plus seeded negative control pass. Fresh npm/Bun installs pass SDK/CLI/MCP, npx/bunx, lifecycle, README/Git/history and telemetry acceptance; packed strict TypeScript consumer passes. Reviewed baseline records the necessary compact omission marker and tightens composite cost."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-17T19:49:25.795Z","harness:codex","Implementation boundary: next owns executable selection in the SDK. The documented selection estimate is the greater of JSON and TOON UTF-8 bytes divided by four; row limits apply first. Alternatives are removed before the recommendation, and infeasible empty envelopes are disclosed honestly. The universal output budget still owns companion queues and the full response. Intent reads omit redundant selection receipts only when no omission or infeasibility needs disclosure."
  "2026-09-17T19:53:49.161Z","harness:codex","All-status tracker health: the resolution validator still flags the 170 historical records explicitly retained as unknown by the completed pm-e9zh evidence-recovery pass; its full notes enumerate the residual and prohibit placeholder backfills. Concurrent validation saw only the two actively edited records as hash mismatches; both immediately passed history --verify --strict-exit with matching current hashes. Final frozen validation will run after all PM writes. Graph redundancy exposes 67 witnessed implied ordering edges; no arbitrary relationships were added to inflate depth."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-17T19:49:27.251Z","harness:codex","Optimizer selection is not delivery evidence. Ranking explanations and usage inclusion must be based on emitted recommendation/ready identifiers. Keep intent receipts lean: an unchanged selection needs no second receipt when the complete-response intent contract already accounts for its cost."
